WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.010
Imagine two woods.

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.310
One has just three kinds of tree.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.870
The other has three hundred.

4
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.210
Then a disease arrives,

5
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.890
and wipes out one kind
of tree in each wood.

6
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.850
Which wood copes better?

7
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.490
And why should the number of
different species make any

8
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.910
difference at all?

9
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.890
In this mission, you'll
meet biodiversity:

10
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.280
the variety of species in an area.

11
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.370
You'll find out what biodiversity
has to do with how stable an

12
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.970
ecosystem is.

13
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.530
And you'll weigh up how a growing
human population puts that

14
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.570
variety under pressure.

15
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.460
Your mission: decide which wood
copes better, and explain why.
